 // tag::body[]
 {manpurpose}
 
-Currently only supports centering floating windows. The `center` argument positions the window in the middle of the screen, taking up 75% of the screen dimensions with equal padding on all sides.
+Supported presets:
+
+- `center`
+- `topLeftCorner`
+- `topRightCorner`
+- `bottomPanel`
+
+The `center` argument positions the window in the middle of the screen, taking up 75% of the screen dimensions with equal padding on all sides.
+`topLeftCorner` and `topRightCorner` place a compact utility window near the top corners.
+`bottomPanel` spans the full width of the monitor along the bottom edge.
 
 If the window is a tiling window, it will first be changed to floating before being positioned.
 
